{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793554439,"nonce":"6CwCAnNXwW9vwRxGN5S/VlULF1c=","title":"Expand and collapse: a closed state rule plus token-timed layout animation","message":"accordion, collapsible and tree expand on springs (persisted animated values, bind_bool_targets) with animate_bounds, and sidebar collapses with animate_bounds and springs. The motion and the closed geometry are Rust.\n\nDo, as ashui: the content carries data-state=\"open|closed\"; a rule closes it (height: 0; overflow: hidden; the sidebar's width from a custom property), and a layout animation eases the size change with the theme's duration-normal and ease-out by default. The chevron turns by a [data-state] rule with a transition. No springs in the widgets.\n\nashui first: components/css/components.css (.ui-collapsible-content[data-state=\"closed\"], .ui-accordion-content[data-state=\"closed\"], .ui-accordion-chevron, .ui-sidebar[data-state=\"collapsed\"]), Accordion.hx / Collapsible.hx / TreeView.hx / Sidebar.hx, and haxe/ashui/animation/LayoutAnimation.hx (timing from theme.animations()).\n\nPart of e4d2db3.","files":null}]}